{"dossier":"D15","entry_points":[{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_file_operations.alt_2","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_read","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_write","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_open","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_poll","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_dir_file_operations.alt_2","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_dir_operations.alt_2","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_inode_operations.alt_2","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_readdir","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_lookup"],"text":"Control files share seek, splice, open, poll and vectored IO; dirs share lookup, permission, attr and iterate with separate node and content tables."},{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_tty.c::tty_drivers_op","fs/proc/proc_tty.c::t_start","fs/proc/proc_tty.c::t_next","fs/proc/proc_tty.c::t_stop","fs/proc/proc_tty.c::show_tty_driver"],"text":"Driver listing is sequential; traversal holds global mutex start to stop, steps with helpers, emits pseudo entries then per-driver ranges split at majors."},{"sids":["fs/proc/self.c::proc_self_get_link","fs/proc/self.c::proc_self_inode_operations","fs/proc/self.c::__ro_after_init","fs/proc/stat.c::stat_proc_ops","fs/proc/stat.c::proc_stat_init"],"text":"Self links resolve caller TGID in namespace, render decimal to short buffer, pinned; stat entry uses sized single-open with seq read, seek and release."},{"sids":["fs/proc/task_mmu.c::proc_maps_open","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::do_maps_open","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::pid_maps_open","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::proc_map_release","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::procfs_procmap_ioctl"],"text":"Maps open allocates seq private state, retains address space with read permission; release drops it; ioctl accepts only procmap query and forwards with captured mm."}],"exports":[{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_init","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::__register_sysctl_init","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::unregister_sysctl_table","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::do_sysctl_args"],"text":"Boot builds sys hierarchy; early register logs failure and pins headers; unregister sleeps, tolerates missing; boot args duplicate cmdline, parse with lazy mount."},{"sids":["fs/proc/root.c::proc_root_init","fs/proc/self.c::proc_self_init","fs/proc/thread_self.c::proc_thread_self_init","fs/proc/proc_tty.c::proc_tty_init","fs/proc/self.c::proc_setup_self","fs/proc/thread_self.c::proc_setup_thread_self","fs/seq_file.c::single_open_size"],"text":"Proc boot prepares pid counts, self numbering, net/fs/driver/bus trees, tty and sys parts, registers fstype last; exposes self/thread installers and sized single-open helper."},{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_tty.c::proc_tty_register_driver","fs/proc/proc_tty.c::proc_tty_unregister_driver","fs/proc/proc_tty.c::proc_tty_driver","fs/read_write.c::kernel_write","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::proc_pid_maps_operations"],"text":"TTY driver entries require name and display support and no existing entry, removed by name; kernel write validates range with accounting; maps file offers seq text plus ioctl."}],"extracts":["5186b84b31e841bcdfc159870d06b36a614a8fd9e1e7c312586aec160de98775","9de307a966a4c31ef2b7acb6dc92f4801bca6786088fc5318cf5154c71fef0a8","d8b709982844c02ed8488edf1bf9b498bf77538e7b6ed304c8af02846d35aabc"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::grab_header","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_revalidate","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_call_handler","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::do_sysctl_args"],"text":"Withdrawal races fixed by pinning, guarded checks, retry and splicing; oversize/alloc/copy/handler/boot failures logged except boot dup which panics."},{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_tty.c::proc_tty_init","fs/proc/root.c::proc_apply_options","fs/proc/root.c::proc_parse_param"],"text":"Serial counts can leak secret length and timing so driver dir is owner-only; live remount changing pidonly or pidns is rejected to avoid inconsistent views."},{"sids":["fs/proc/task_mmu.c::proc_get_vma","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::do_procmap_query","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::procfs_procmap_ioctl"],"text":"Contention retries after upgrade; lock, task/mm, query, alloc, name, copy and ioctl faults each map to distinct errors with cleanup of refs, buffers and files."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["fs/proc/root.c::proc_param","fs/proc/root.c::proc_fs_parameters","include/linux/fs_parser.h::fsparam_u32","include/linux/fs_parser.h::fs_parse","fs/proc/root.c::proc_parse_param","include/linux/fs_context.h::invalfc","fs/proc/root.c::valid_hidepid","fs/proc/root.c::proc_parse_hidepid_param","fs/proc/root.c::proc_parse_subset_param","fs/proc/root.c::proc_parse_pidns_param"],"text":"Mount accepts gid, hidepid, subset, pidns; hidepid allows four levels or aliases; subset allows only pid; pidns needs nsfs object, caps and descendant check."},{"sids":["fs/proc/root.c::proc_apply_options","fs/proc/root.c::proc_fill_super","fs/proc/root.c::proc_root_lookup","fs/proc/root.c::proc_root_readdir","fs/proc/root.c::proc_root_getattr"],"text":"Superblock sets noexec, small block, magic, no stacking/shrink, root/self links; root lookup tries pid first, readdir delegates after static entries, getattr adds live count."},{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::test_perm","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_perm","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_permission","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_setattr","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_getattr","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_make_inode"],"text":"Access needs all classes in privileged tier, denies exec and root writes; mode/owner changes rejected, attrs overlay live mode; nodes get fresh id, bind header/table."},{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_follow_link","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_link_fill_cache","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_is_seen","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_compare","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_revalidate","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_delete","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::process_sysctl_arg","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_find_alias","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_is_alias","include/linux/fs.h::file_open_root_mnt"],"text":"Links retarget via set translation and name search with ref exchange; withdrawing headers are invalid/deletable and hidden; boot args accept two separators, aliases, need value, log errors."},{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_call_handler","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_open","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_poll"],"text":"Transfer requires handler and size ceiling, uses zeroed bounce area with control-program adjustment, delegates to handler with position; open captures poll generation, poll signals on change."},{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::setup_sysctl_set","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::retire_sysctl_set","fs/seq_file.c::seq_list_start","fs/seq_file.c::seq_list_next"],"text":"Set init clears set, records visibility predicate, links dir header to root table; retire asserts empty tree; seq list helpers walk by zero-based position and null at wrap."},{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_tty.c::show_tty_range","fs/proc/stat.c::show_irq_gap","fs/proc/stat.c::show_all_irqs","fs/proc/stat.c::show_stat","fs/proc/stat.c::stat_open","fs/proc/stat.c::arch_irq_stat_cpu","fs/proc/softirqs.c::show_softirqs","fs/proc/softirqs.c::proc_softirqs_init"],"text":"Range display shows identity, base name, major/minor span and type wording with fallback; stat aggregates per-CPU times, irqs, switches, boot time and counts; softirqs prints per-CPU matrix."},{"sids":["fs/proc/task_mmu.c::get_vma_name","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::show_vma_header_prefix","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::show_map_vma","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::show_map","include/linux/fs.h::file_user_inode"],"text":"Mapping names prefer file path unless anon override, then driver, arch, vdso, heap/stack markers; header encodes range, four access chars, offset, dev numbers and inode plus name."},{"sids":["fs/proc/task_mmu.c::do_procmap_query","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::query_matching_vma"],"text":"Query selects covering or next meeting filters; validates sizing/flags/pairs; on success returns bounds, perms, page size, file ids and optional truncated name/id after unlock."},{"sids":["fs/proc/task_mmu.c::smaps_page_accumulate","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::smaps_account","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::smaps_pte_entry","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::smaps_pte_hole_lookup","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::smaps_pmd_entry.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::smaps_pmd_entry.alt_2","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::smaps_pte_hole.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::smaps_pte_hole.alt_2"],"text":"PSS splits by anon/shmem/file plus locked/dirty/shared; pte handles present/hole/swap/device; THP classifies large folios; holes charge shmem swap or nothing."}],"locks":[{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_make_inode","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_is_seen","fs/proc/proc_tty.c::t_start","fs/proc/proc_tty.c::t_stop"],"text":"Central spin guard covers withdrawal checks, linkage, link exchange and visibility; driver collection mutex is held from traversal start to stop."},{"sids":["fs/proc/task_mmu.c::hold_task_mempolicy.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::release_task_mempolicy.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::hold_task_mempolicy.alt_2","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::release_task_mempolicy.alt_2","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::lock_ctx_mm.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::unlock_ctx_mm.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::reset_lock_ctx","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::unlock_ctx_vma","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::lock_vma_range.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::unlock_vma_range.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::unlock_ctx_mm.alt_2"],"text":"One build locks task around policy capture with ref release, other is empty; maps ctx tracks mm flag and pinned vma, uses interruptible read lock with reset semantics."},{"sids":["fs/proc/task_mmu.c::get_next_vma.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::fallback_to_mmap_lock.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::drop_rcu.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::reacquire_rcu.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::lock_ctx_mm.alt_2","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::lock_vma_range.alt_2","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::get_next_vma.alt_2","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::fallback_to_mmap_lock.alt_2","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::query_vma_setup.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::query_vma_teardown.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::query_vma_find_by_addr.alt_1","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::query_vma_setup.alt_2","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::query_vma_teardown.alt_2","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::query_vma_find_by_addr.alt_2"],"text":"One maps config always holds mm read lock; other prefers per-vma under RCU and upgrades irreversibly on contention. Query setup/teardown pair protections; lookup upgrades on overflow."},{"sids":["fs/proc/task_mmu.c::m_start","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::m_stop"],"text":"Iteration start retains task and mm refs then takes policy and range locks; stop releases policy, mm and task and clears cache, no-op when no task held."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p10","crown":"A","phase":"F5"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::grab_header","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::scan","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::proc_sys_fill_cache","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_follow_link"],"text":"Header pins are taken on lookup/create/transfer with default-set fallback, exchanged on link switch, released on exit; dir reads emit dots then live entries by index."},{"sids":["fs/proc/root.c::proc_init_fs_context","fs/proc/root.c::proc_fs_context_free","fs/proc/root.c::proc_reconfigure","fs/proc/root.c::proc_get_tree","fs/proc/root.c::proc_fs_context_ops","fs/proc/root.c::proc_kill_sb","fs/proc/root.c::proc_fs_type"],"text":"Context starts bound to caller pidns, parses options repeatedly, then builds fresh superblock or reconfigures live one; teardown releases ns and cred refs."},{"sids":["fs/proc/task_mmu.c::m_start","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::m_next","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::m_stop","fs/proc/task_mmu.c::proc_get_vma"],"text":"Maps iteration start/next/stop: end sentinel terminates, gate yields gate mapping, else first mapping at offset; next advances to gate then end; stop balances all holdings."}],"structs":[{"sids":["fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_alias","fs/proc/proc_sysctl.c::sysctl_aliases"],"text":"Alias records pair legacy kernel parameter spelling with dotted control pa